From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mzak <mzak.amin@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 21:54:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 104/117] serial: qcom-geni: keep the port IRQ masked across
 system sleep

Clearing pending interrupts while suspended (commit "serial: qcom-geni:
Clear pending IRQs while suspended") handles the early IRQ_NONE race in
the shutdown path, but the TTY wakeup path can skip shutdown() and leave
the port IRQ enabled until pm_runtime_force_suspend() removes the
register power. An interrupt in that window reads a powered-off serial
engine and is reported as unhandled, and enough of them disable the
line, which takes the Bluetooth UART down.

Mask the port IRQ for the whole system sleep transition, with a disable
depth of its own that is independent of startup() / shutdown(): taken
before uart_suspend_port(), released after uart_resume_port(), kept if
the force resume fails but never taken twice, and released again when
the suspend callback itself fails (the PM core does not resume a device
whose suspend failed). A no_console_suspend console keeps its IRQ.

Analysis and approach by yzddmr6 (af2a6e2a5153 "serial: qcom-geni: mask
the IRQ across the complete sleep transition", itself a cross-check of a
Xiaomi Pad 6 Pro fix; no Signed-off-by); re-implemented.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: mzak <mzak.amin@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/tty/serial/qcom_geni_serial.c | 46 +++++++++++++++++++++++----
 1 file changed, 39 insertions(+), 7 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/tty/serial/qcom_geni_serial.c b/drivers/tty/serial/qcom_geni_serial.c
index e5d1e7679c648..0f45ffd91c616 100644
--- a/drivers/tty/serial/qcom_geni_serial.c
+++ b/drivers/tty/serial/qcom_geni_serial.c
@@ -139,6 +139,8 @@ struct qcom_geni_serial_port {
 	dma_addr_t tx_dma_addr;
 	dma_addr_t rx_dma_addr;
 	bool setup;
+	/* the port IRQ is masked for a system sleep transition */
+	bool sleep_irq_masked;
 	unsigned long poll_timeout_us;
 	unsigned long clk_rate;
 	void *rx_buf;
@@ -2080,6 +2082,15 @@ static int __maybe_unused qcom_geni_serial_runtime_resume(struct device *dev)
 	return 0;
 }
 
+static void qcom_geni_serial_unmask_sleep_irq(struct qcom_geni_serial_port *port)
+{
+	if (!port->sleep_irq_masked)
+		return;
+
+	port->sleep_irq_masked = false;
+	enable_irq(port->uport.irq);
+}
+
 static int qcom_geni_serial_suspend(struct device *dev)
 {
 	struct qcom_geni_serial_port *port = dev_get_drvdata(dev);
@@ -2096,18 +2107,38 @@ static int qcom_geni_serial_suspend(struct device *dev)
 		geni_icc_set_bw(&port->se);
 	}
 
-	ret = uart_suspend_port(private_data->drv, uport);
-	if (ret)
-		return ret;
-
 	/*
 	 * When no_console_suspend is set the console must remain active
-	 * across system sleep, so skip the force suspend path.
+	 * across system sleep, its IRQ included, so skip the force suspend
+	 * path.
 	 */
 	if (!console_suspend_enabled && uart_console(uport))
-		return 0;
+		return uart_suspend_port(private_data->drv, uport);
+
+	/*
+	 * Mask the port IRQ for the whole transition: the TTY wakeup path can
+	 * skip shutdown() and leave it enabled until the force suspend removes
+	 * the register power, and an interrupt then finds a powered-off serial
+	 * engine and is counted as unhandled. This disable depth is separate
+	 * from startup() / shutdown(); it stays if a resume fails, but is
+	 * never taken twice.
+	 */
+	if (!port->sleep_irq_masked) {
+		disable_irq(uport->irq);
+		port->sleep_irq_masked = true;
+	}
 
-	return pm_runtime_force_suspend(dev);
+	ret = uart_suspend_port(private_data->drv, uport);
+	if (!ret) {
+		ret = pm_runtime_force_suspend(dev);
+		if (!ret)
+			return 0;
+		/* The PM core does not resume a device whose suspend failed. */
+		uart_resume_port(private_data->drv, uport);
+	}
+
+	qcom_geni_serial_unmask_sleep_irq(port);
+	return ret;
 }
 
 static int qcom_geni_serial_resume(struct device *dev)
@@ -2130,6 +2161,7 @@ static int qcom_geni_serial_resume(struct device *dev)
 	}
 
 	ret = uart_resume_port(private_data->drv, uport);
+	qcom_geni_serial_unmask_sleep_irq(port);
 	if (uart_console(uport)) {
 		geni_icc_set_tag(&port->se, QCOM_ICC_TAG_ALWAYS);
 		geni_icc_set_bw(&port->se);
-- 
